From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Charlie <5764343+charlielye@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 06:24:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] refactor(foundation): one Poseidon2 implementation, typed on
 Fr[]

The asynchronous poseidon module's synchronous branch duplicated crypto/sync. Now
both modules have the same two layers: functions on Fr[] (poseidon2HashFields,
poseidon2PermutationFields, poseidon2AbsorbChain) and the Fieldable wrappers over
them. The asynchronous module's synchronous branch calls the sync module's
functions; only its asynchronous branch has code of its own. The byte chunking and
the absorb-chain command, shared by both, move to poseidon/encoding.ts. A test
checks that every function hashes the same synchronously and asynchronously.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015HXzMEGRnmFYs5yXRcAWCb

